From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mfd: syscon: Add the Allwinner A733 SERDES top
 registers

One 4 KiB page of the SERDES block of the A733 holds the protocol and
lane muxes of both combo PHYs: the DisplayPort lane width conversion and
the USB3 PIPE clock and RX data muxes of the first combo PHY, and the
PIPE TX data mux of the second. Each PHY driver writes its own
registers, but the page cannot be split between the two PHY nodes.

Add the page as a system controller, so that both PHYs reach it through
a phandle and a shared regmap.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; both combo PHYs reach
their registers through the node as a syscon, and the registers read
back the values the PHYs program.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
index 945a168b613d..937199157b51 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ properties:
               - allwinner,sun8i-h3-system-controller
               - allwinner,sun8i-v3s-system-controller
               - allwinner,sun50i-a64-system-controller
+              - allwinner,sun60i-a733-serdes-top
               - altr,l3regs
               - altr,sdr-ctl
               - amd,pensando-elba-syscon
